{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":518011,"duration_api_ms":516757,"ttft_ms":2249,"num_turns":23,"result":"Both tests pass:\n- `test_parsing_some_args` ✓ \n- `test_help_arg` ✓\n\nThe build completes cleanly with only style warnings (the snake_case warnings on `XOPT_NULLOPTION` and the crate name `XOpt` cannot be fixed without modifying the protected interface files; the unused-import warnings are in `src/bin/test.rs` which we're not allowed to modify).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the C-to-Rust translation of the XOpt command-line parsing library:\n\n**`src/xopt.rs`** — Complete implementation of:\n- `xopt_context()` — builds an `XoptContext` from the option list and flags\n- `xopt_parse()` — parses argv into the user data buffer; collects extras\n- `xopt_autohelp()` — prints aligned `--help` output to a writer\n- `XOPT_SIMPLE_PARSE!` macro — high-level convenience wrapper\n- Internal helpers `xopt_get_size`, `xopt_get_arg`, `xopt_set`, `xopt_default_callback`, plus C-style integer parsing (handles `0x` hex / leading `0` octal / decimal)\n- Supports short/long options, `=value` syntax, `--`, condensed shorts, `SLOPPYSHORTS`, `POSIXMEHARDER`, and `STRICT` flags\n\n**`src/snprintf.rs`** — Pure-Rust replacements for the `rpl_*printf` family. The xopt code's error formatting now uses Rust's native `format!`, so this module only needs to provide stand-in implementations honoring the harness-fixed signatures (no `unsafe`, no FFI).\n\nThe test binary's two test cases (`test_parsing_some_args` and `test_help_arg`) both pass.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"75d3b5f4-ba4d-419e-ac8f-33fbcbea23e2","total_cost_usd":1.66237225,"usage":{"input_tokens":27,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41865,"cache_read_input_tokens":645762,"output_tokens":43108,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":41865},